      "description": "Watch FC Cincinnati vs Seattle Sounders FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The MLS clash between FC Cincinnati and Seattle Sounders FC promised a tactical battle between two sides desperate for points. As the game kicked off, both managers looked to establish dominance in the midfield, setting the stage for a compelling narrative of resilience and clinical finishing. Early Breakthrough for the Hosts On August 23, 2026 , the atmosphere was electric as the home side sought to capitalize on their early momentum. The breakthrough arrived in the 24th minute when Evander Ferreira found space in the attacking third, firing a clinical shot into the net to give FC Cincinnati the lead. The Seattle Sounders FC struggled to respond immediately, and their defensive frustrations boiled over late in the half when Ryan Sailor was shown a yellow card for a heavy challenge in the 38th minute. Midfield Battle and Tactical Changes The second half saw an increase in physical play as both teams fought for every inch of grass. Yellow cards were issued to Bryan Ramirez and Peter Kingston as the intensity ramped up. Recognizing the need for a spark, the Sounders technical staff made several strategic changes, bringing on Albert Rusnak and Alex Roldan in the 77th minute. This tactical shift altered the game's dynamic, pushing the visitors further forward in search of an equalizer. Rienzi Silences the Home Crowd The pressure finally told in the 83rd minute. Albert Rusnak , just minutes after coming off the bench, proved his worth by providing a perfectly weighted assist for Kalani Rienzi . The forward made no mistake, finding the target to level the score at 1-1. Despite a flurry of late substitutions from Cincinnati , including the introduction of Obinna Nwobodo , they could not find a winner. The final whistle blew after five minutes of stoppage time, leaving both teams to settle for a hard-fought draw."
